<title>SINGAPORE: TABLE - TLB H1 net up 62 pct to S$3.4 mln.</title>
<headline>TABLE - TLB H1 net up 62 pct to S$3.4 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     3.42  vs  2.12</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		     1.85  vs  1.18</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		    4.56  vs  7.06</p>
<p>    Turnover				 8.08  vs  8.73</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	0.89  vs  0.51</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		   2.94  vs  2.34</p>
<p>    Depreciation and amortisation    0.48  vs  0.50</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 4.85  vs  3.94</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	    0.02  vs  0.07</p>
<p>    Tax					1.50  vs  2.02</p>
<p>    Minorities			     0.05  vs  0.14</p>
<p>Dividend pay date: October 8, 1997</p>
<p>Last day books open: September 23, 1997</p>
<p>Note - TLB Land Ltd was formerly known as Pan Malayan Holdings Ltd. The company said profits were boosted by the sale of short term Australian quoted investments and an increase in rental income from a Melbourne property.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (65) 870-3080; Fax (65) 776-8112</p>
